<title>UK: CRICKET-BENSON AND HEDGES CUP RESULTS/SCORES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-BENSON AND HEDGES CUP RESULTS/SCORES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results and latest scores in</p>
<p>Benson and Hedges Cup (50 overs) first round cricket matches on</p>
<p>Monday:</p>
<p>At Chelmsford: Essex beat Glamorgan by five wickets.</p>
<p>Glamorgan 210 In 49.3 overs (H.Morris 67). Essex 211-5 in 41.3</p>
<p>overs (R.Irani 82 not out).</p>
<p>At Bristol: Gloucestershire beat British Universities by 122</p>
<p>runs. Gloucestershire 281-6 innings closed (N. Trainor 62,</p>
<p>S.Young 52; R.Martin-Jenkins 4-57). British Universities 159 in</p>
<p>49.1 overs (T.Bailey 52; M.Ball 4-23).</p>
<p>At The Oval: Kent beat Surrey by four wickets. Surrey 257 in</p>
<p>49.5 overs (A.Stewart 51; M.Fleming 5-54). Kent 262-6 innings</p>
<p>closed (M.Walker 56).</p>
<p>At Hove: Sussex beat Hampshire by 49 runs. Sussex 232-7</p>
<p>innings closed (C.Athey 66). Hampshire 183 in 47.3 overs</p>
<p>(J.Stephenson 65).</p>
<p>At Worcester: Warwickshire beat Worcestershire by six</p>
<p>wickets. Worcestershire 96 in 37.1 overs (D.Brown 5-31) v</p>
<p>Warwickshire 97-4 in 30.2 overs.</p>
<p>At Leicester: Leicestershire beat Scotland by 178 runs.</p>
<p>Leicestershire 371-6 innings closed (D.Maddy 97, I. Sutcliffe</p>
<p>59, A.Habib 53, J.Whitaker 51). Scotland 193-6 innings closed.</p>
<p>The following matches were interupted by rain and will resume</p>
<p>on Tuesday:</p>
<p>In Dublin: Ireland 281-4 innings closed (W.Cronje 94 not out,</p>
<p>J.Curry 75). Middlesex 134-6 in 32.2 overs.</p>
<p>At Old Trafford: Yorkshire 43-0 in 10.5 overs v Lancashire.</p>
<p>At Lakenham: Minor Counties 256-7 innings closed (R. Dalton</p>
<p>76, M.Fell 67). Derbyshire 166-2 in 32.2 overs (C.Adams 95 not</p>
<p>out).</p>
<p>At Trent Bridge: Durham 230-5 innings closed (D.Boon 64 not</p>
<p>out). Nottinghamshire 94-3 in 26 overs.</p>
</text>
